# DESK30 -- make a desktop shortcut, then save the desktop.
#
#   B_WIN1       the C:\ window open
#   C_DRAGGING   QED.NAP held over empty desktop surface, right of the window
#   D_SHORTCUT   released: the shortcut icon stands on the desktop
#   E_SAVED      after Options -> Save desktop (the #X line is on the card)
#
# Coordinates from d-probe: 'QED.NAP' in window 1 box (141,255) -> click
# (179,271); window 1 is (48,43,544,400), i.e. y <= 442, so the strip below it
# is desktop surface and the bottom icon row there is free between the trash
# (0,433) and the printer (546,433). Menu: title 3 (Options) hovers at (196,9),
# 'Save desktop...' clicks at (280,187).
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 37 42
1700 down
1703 up
1710 down
1713 up
2300 move 600 240
3000 mark B_WIN1
3400 move 179 271
3700 down
3800 drag 250 458
4100 mark C_DRAGGING
4600 up
4800 move 600 300
5400 mark D_SHORTCUT
5800 move 196 9
6200 move 280 187
6400 down
6403 up
6800 move 600 300
7400 mark E_SAVED
